<title>USA: Texas GO bonds repriced, Alex. Brown lowers yield.</title>
<headline>Texas GO bonds repriced, Alex. Brown lowers yield.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alex. Brown &amp; Sons Inc said Wednesday it repriced Texas's $47.9 million Veterans' Housing Assistance Program bonds, lowering the yield in 2014 to 5.40 percent from 5.45 percent. The 2020 and 2026 maturities were not formally reoffered at the repricing.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>RE: $47,930,000*</p>
<p>STATE OF TEXAS GO</p>
<p>Veterans' Housing Assistance Program</p>
<p>Fund II Series 1995 E</p>
<p>Refunding Bonds</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>REMARKETING</p>
<p>SUBJECT TO ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aa		    S&amp;P: AA</p>
<p>    DATED: 11/06/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 06/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>12/01/2014		8,130M    5.40  %	100.00</p>
<p>12/01/2020	     16,310M	NRO	     -</p>
<p>12/01/2026	     23,490M	NRO	     -</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 12/01/2006    102.00</p>
<p>		   DTP 12/01/2010</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected on Thursay, October 24, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on November 6, 1996.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
<p>Alex. Brown &amp; Son Incorporated</p>
<p>Smith Barney Inc.</p>
<p>Prudential Securities Incorporated</p>
<p>Artemis Capital Group, Inc.</p>
<p>Walton Johnson &amp; Company</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
